{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1360478-martial-arts-with-perfect-defenses-in-exalted-2nd-edition","id":1360478,"title":"Martial Arts with Perfect Defenses in Exalted 2nd Edition???","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-01-12T02:08:11-08:00","id":1360478,"title":"<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/icons/icon5.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" /> Martial Arts with Perfect Defenses in Exalted 2nd Edition???","content":"I am very old, now, &amp; I can't remember all the MA styles in 2nd (or 2.5) Edition that had Perfect Defenses.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://external-content.duckduckgo.com/iu/?u=http%3A%2F%2Fi.ytimg.com%2Fvi%2FlEls6pJOUPw%2Fhqdefault.jpg&amp;f=1&amp;nofb=1\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> I vaguely recall Swaying Grass Style being a rare TMA with one, and Crane &amp; one of the Virtue Styles having one.<br /> <br /> I never got why every one of the 5 Immaculate Styles didn't have PDs. That always struck me as a major oversight on the Sidreals' part.<br /> <br /> Every-time I read how the Sidreals want to revise the Immaculate Dragon Styles, I think <span style=\"color:#2F4F4F\">&quot;Yeah! You should! Because you made them without PD's &amp; then sicced the poor bastards on 300 Lunars,</span><i><span style=\"color:#2F4F4F\"> ya crazy Swedes!&quot;</span></i> Seriously. There is no excuse for this level of incompetency &amp; lack of foresight from the Martial Arts Exalts.<br /> <br /> BRONZE FACTION: <span style=\"color:#800000\">&quot;Duh... why Dragon Bloods have such hard time with LUNARS &amp; Faries &amp; siznit??? They are such lame replacements for the Solars we had them murder. If only we could do something 'bout it. Durp durp.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> Goold Faction: <span style=\"color:#FF8C00\">&quot;Wow. Let's just let them slowly hang themselves until we get an original idea. Maybe we should, you know, free the Solars Exaltations or something if we are going to hang onto the title of 'Gold Faction.' Or we can be passive-aggressive jerks that milk this to be different &amp; pretend to be rebellious for countless centuries.&quot; </span><br /> <br /> Sidreals are so dumb. Writing this post made me realize it. They are just brilliantly dumb.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4428,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4428-daredevil","user":"Daredevil","date":". 01-12-2020, 03:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4428-daredevil","name":"Daredevil","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4428_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"404"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-12T02:31:44-08:00","id":1360479,"title":"","content":"Water Dragon has a perfect defence: Bottomless Depths Defense, IIRC.<br /> <br /> prototype00","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-12T03:40:53-08:00","id":1360485,"title":"","content":"Also, just because you can design a thing, doesn\u2019t mean that thing can be made. I can design a building made out of Adamantium, but I won\u2019t be building it until that portal to the Marvel universe gets finished.<br /> <br /> Making a style that resonates with a Dragon-Blooded in such a harmonious way <i>and</i> having it include easily-accessible perfect defenses might not have been doable (with Water Dragon being a happy accident); their failure to do the impossible does not make them stupid.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 01-12-2020, 06:42 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-12T03:49:28-08:00","id":1360490,"title":"","content":"2.5 combat revolves heavily around PDs, but it wasn\u2019t necessarily meant to do that. It was probably the intent of the early designers to make splats without PDs viable, it just didn\u2019t work out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-12T04:36:50-08:00","id":1360494,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Daredevil</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1360478-martial-arts-with-perfect-defenses-in-exalted-2nd-edition#post1360478\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I never got why every one of the 5 Dragon Styles didn't have PDs. That always struck me as a major oversight on the Sidreals' part.</div> </div> </div> </div>Because 2e Dragon-Blooded needing a perfect defence and having to reach outside their charmset to get one is a much bigger failure on behalf of the writers.<br /> Ten Thousand Corrections tried to fix it but it suffered from that weird mindlock where 2e writers were afraid to simply retract contradictory statements in favour of Obi Wan style truths. So rather than ignoring &quot;as close as mere Terrestrial Exalt can come to a perfect melee defence&quot; they built a teamwork perfect defence on top of it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-12T07:04:09-08:00","id":1360509,"title":"","content":"<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>prototype00</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1360478-martial-arts-with-perfect-defenses-in-exalted-2nd-edition?p=1360479#post1360479\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Water Dragon has a perfect defence: Bottomless Depths Defense, IIRC.</div> </div> </div> </div>I know what you are thinking, but I do not suffer from dementia. My nurse mixed up my meds this morning, &amp; made me confused. I should have followed my own advise &amp; never let in a nurse hired by my kids. I knew they are trying to kill me.<br /> <img src=\"https://external-content.duckduckgo.com/iu/?u=http%3A%2F%2Fvignette3.wikia.nocookie.net%2Fvillains%2Fimages%2F9%2F99%2FDavid_Lo-Pan_3.png%2Frevision%2Flatest%2Fscale-to-width-down%2F250%3Fcb%3D20130329213946&amp;f=1&amp;nofb=1\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1360478-martial-arts-with-perfect-defenses-in-exalted-2nd-edition?p=1360485#post1360485\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can design a building made out of Adamantium, but I won\u2019t be building it until that portal to the Marvel universe gets finished.</div> </div> </div> </div>You paint pretty pictures, my friend.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1360478-martial-arts-with-perfect-defenses-in-exalted-2nd-edition?p=1360485#post1360485\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Making a style that resonates with a Dragon-Blooded in such a harmonious way <i>and</i> having it include easily-accessible perfect defenses might not have been doable (with Water Dragon being a happy accident); their failure to do the impossible does not make them stupid.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sidereal Apologist. There, I said it! Sidereal apologist!<br /> <br /> Disavow!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1360478-martial-arts-with-perfect-defenses-in-exalted-2nd-edition?p=1360490#post1360490\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2.5 combat revolves heavily around PDs, but it wasn\u2019t necessarily meant to do that. It was probably the intent of the early designers to make splats without PDs viable, it just didn\u2019t work out.</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel like I am getting the same vibe while reading the earlier material. How do you think they intended that to work in practice?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1360478-martial-arts-with-perfect-defenses-in-exalted-2nd-edition?p=1360494#post1360494\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because 2e Dragon-Blooded needing a perfect defence and having to reach outside their charmset to get one is a much bigger failure on behalf of the writers.</div> </div> </div> </div>I kind of get it from the writers\u2019 perspective if they were going with the idea of Celestial Martial Arts being a way to transform a being of a lower level of \u201cenlightenment,\u201d &amp; elevating them to something closure to Celestial might.<br /> <br /> This of course has it\u2019s issues in that it makes MA the mandatory go to for Dragon Blooded Player Characters &amp; major NPC\u2019s, but I can see an appeal in the theme.<br /> <br /> It also highlights the idea of the Sidereals using MA in general to \u2018hack\u2019 the Dragon Blooded &amp; make them better replacements for the Solars. Still not perfect, but better.<br /> <br /> Heck, in early 2nd Material they did not forbid Dragon Blooded from learning Sidereal MA (no Earth shattering Ka-Boom!), &amp; noted that when a DB finally learns that level of MA they will be transformed into a newer being. I am insanely curious what those writers had in mind. Enlightened super powers are a topic I enjoy reading about.<br /> <br /> Does anyone have any ideas on what you think might be an interesting evolution for a DB with SMA?<br /> <br /> OMG, I\u2019m a writer apologist!<br /> <br /> I disavow myself.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1360478-martial-arts-with-perfect-defenses-in-exalted-2nd-edition?p=1360494#post1360494\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ten Thousand Corrections tried to fix it but it suffered from that weird mindlock where 2e writers were afraid to simply retract contradictory statements in favour of Obi Wan style truths. So rather than ignoring &quot;as close as mere Terrestrial Exalt can come to a perfect melee defence&quot; they built a teamwork perfect defence on top of it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I forgot about that addition. I\u2019ll have to look that one up. Thank you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4428,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4428-daredevil","user":"Daredevil","date":". 01-12-2020, 03:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4428-daredevil","name":"Daredevil","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4428_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"404"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-12T07:04:10-08:00","id":1360510,"title":"","content":"I see these PD being talked about every now and then. I'm not interested in going too deep into 2ed to understand the discussion so what does it do approximately ? You just activate the Charm and are immune to every attack for the round ?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-12T07:08:54-08:00","id":1360511,"title":"","content":"Edit: Actually its been a while, I'm not sure about the reset thing for 2.5.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-12T08:18:06-08:00","id":1360521,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>prototype00</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1360478-martial-arts-with-perfect-defenses-in-exalted-2nd-edition?p=1360511#post1360511\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Edit: Actually its been a while, I'm not sure about the reset thing for 2.5.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wouldn't mind reading your evaluation of 2.0. It's were it all began, after all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4428-daredevil","name":"Daredevil","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4428_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"404"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-12T09:12:51-08:00","id":1360529,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Daredevil</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1360478-martial-arts-with-perfect-defenses-in-exalted-2nd-edition?p=1360509#post1360509\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel like I am getting the same vibe while reading the earlier material. How do you think they intended that to work in practice?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well in 1e Heavenly Guardian Defense actually cost a willpower to use. The intent might have been to use PDs only against very dangerous attacks, but without a full understanding of just how easy it was to make an attack incredibly dangerous and maybe how cheap they really were. Dipping Swallow was 2m still, so like, for 1 extra mote instead of ignoring all penalties to your DV you just blocked the attack perfectly.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1360478-martial-arts-with-perfect-defenses-in-exalted-2nd-edition?p=1360510#post1360510\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I see these PD being talked about every now and then. I'm not interested in going too deep into 2ed to understand the discussion so what does it do approximately ? You just activate the Charm and are immune to every attack for the round ?</div> </div> </div> </div>A perfect defense comes in 3 main forms, perfect parry, perfect dodge and perfect soak. The first two effectively set your Defence Value to infinite against one attack, parrying it or dodging it no matter the successes they rolled, the last one negated all damage from the attack but didn't negate other effects like an on-hit knockdown or something. It only works for one instant, so one attack, but they were cheap, like 3m cheap. It was literally cheaper to perfectly defend than it was to raise your defense by 2 with the excellency.<br /> <br /> The only down side was that they had to have what was called a &quot;Flaw of Invulnerability&quot;. These were essentially meaningless though, in most cases. The Flaw of Invulnerability for Conviction stated that you couldn't use it if the actions were contrary to the characters primary motivation, which is like their single greatest defining intimacy.<br /> <br /> It was also really really damn easy to make attacks that were super deadly. There were even perfect attacks that always hit unless blocked by a perfect defense. Which lead to basically everything revolving around perfects. You could beat a perfect by just attacking 5 times in a single tick with charms, they'd have to perfect every attack, but there were also flurry-breaker charms that let you block the attack and then get away instantly to avoid being flurried more.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-12T09:15:33-08:00","id":1360531,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1360478-martial-arts-with-perfect-defenses-in-exalted-2nd-edition?p=1360510#post1360510\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I see these PD being talked about every now and then. I'm not interested in going too deep into 2ed to understand the discussion so what does it do approximately ? You just activate the Charm and are immune to every attack for the round ?</div> </div> </div> </div>In 2nd ed, Solar Dodge had (Dodge 4, 1 prereqcharm) Seven Shadow Evasion: 3m, dodge an attack without any roll. In 3rd ed, it still exists, but it's 1/fight and costs wp.<br /> So, every time you were attacked, you did a stunt (regenerating 2-4m, occasionally 6) and spent 3m, and... didn't get hit.<br /> There was also a 4m version in Melee.<br /> Notice how if you were good at stunting, you were impossible to hit but didn't actually go down motes.<br /> Thus, the only way to kill Solars was unexpected attacks or making multiple attacks at once.<br /> <br /> Other splats mostly had equivalents that were marginally pricier.<br /> <br /> It's also important to note that an unarmoured exalt hit with a grand goremaul would probably take about 16 dice of lethal (not Withering, lethal), and the wielder could do that every round.<br /> <br /> It was a combat system that was really dangerous unless you had a perfect defence, but really easy if you did. So not very fun.<br /> <br /> Admittedly, it tended to be fine when social Dragonblood duelled with their swords, or armoured Dragonblood fought with daiklaives (as long as they didn't use multi-attack charms since they were so slow) but any combat-built Celestial was likely to make a fight boring. At least, that's my experience.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-12T09:25:35-08:00","id":1360533,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1360478-martial-arts-with-perfect-defenses-in-exalted-2nd-edition?p=1360529#post1360529\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The <b>only</b> down side was that they had to have what was called a &quot;Flaw of Invulnerability&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>They also tended to make fights rather boring, as it would almost invariably result in a series of no-sells until one person runs out of motes, at which point they either get splattered in one hit, or enter a Death Spiral from which recovery is almost impossible.<br /> <br /> \u200bI consider that a downside.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-12T09:57:32-08:00","id":1360541,"title":"","content":"Yeah okay seems like an interesting idea with poor execution","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-12T10:00:08-08:00","id":1360543,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1360478-martial-arts-with-perfect-defenses-in-exalted-2nd-edition?p=1360533#post1360533\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They also tended to make fights rather boring, as it would almost invariably result in a series of no-sells until one person runs out of motes, at which point they either get splattered in one hit, or enter a Death Spiral from which recovery is almost impossible.<br /> <br /> \u200bI consider that a downside.</div> </div> </div> </div>For the joy of the game, yes, but not really a downside to the effectiveness of the charm.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-12T12:54:12-08:00","id":1360573,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Daredevil</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1360478-martial-arts-with-perfect-defenses-in-exalted-2nd-edition#post1360478\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">one of the Virtue Styles having one.</div> </div> </div> </div>To be specific, the Art of Meditative Discussion (i.e. the Temperance style) had one (Untouchable Purpose).<br /> <br /> 2m, 1w isn't so bad for an applicability-trumping perfect defense, but I'm not a big fan of the Temperance Flaw of Invulnerability.<br /> <br /> ...Huh. I just noticed that the Scroll of Errata never touched on that Charm in the 2.5 update (back when most perfect defenses went to 8m). I guess the writers didn't have time for every oddball supplement.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11237-jefepato","name":"Jefepato","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11237_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"557"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-12T13:18:56-08:00","id":1360579,"title":"","content":"Note it was one Sidereal who made all 5 and she did more to improve the Dragon-Blooded than 300 Solars did during the 3000+ years when they worked for them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/535-bastet","name":"Bastet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar535_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-13T09:45:59-08:00","id":1360700,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jefepato</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1360478-martial-arts-with-perfect-defenses-in-exalted-2nd-edition?p=1360573#post1360573\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> To be specific, the Art of Meditative Discussion (i.e. the Temperance style) had one (Untouchable Purpose).<br /> <br /> 2m, 1w isn't so bad for an applicability-trumping perfect defense, but I'm not a big fan of the Temperance Flaw of Invulnerability.<br /> <br /> ...Huh. I just noticed that the Scroll of Errata never touched on that Charm in the 2.5 update (back when most perfect defenses went to 8m). I guess the writers didn't have time for every oddball supplement.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you!<br /> <br /> So far we have:<br /> <br /> <b>Untouchable Purpose</b> [The Art of Meditative Discussion (\u201cTemperance Style\u201d), The Imperfect Lotus - Page 18]<br /> <br /> <b>Bottomless Depths Defense</b> [Water Dragon Style, MoEP: The Dragon Blooded- Page 209]<br /> <br /> Does Crossed Wings Denial [<b>Crane Style</b>] exist in 2nd Edition? I can't find it in any of my books, &amp; it's making me wounder if I have had a mini-stroke last night.<br /> <img src=\"https://external-content.duckduckgo.com/iu/?u=https%3A%2F%2Fvignette.wikia.nocookie.net%2Fvillains%2Fimages%2Fa%2Fa5%2FLo-Pan%2527s_death.png%2Frevision%2Flatest%2Fscale-to-width-down%2F300%3Fcb%3D20130329214541&amp;f=1&amp;nofb=1\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4428,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4428-daredevil","user":"Daredevil","date":". 01-13-2020, 12:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4428-daredevil","name":"Daredevil","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4428_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"404"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-13T10:22:52-08:00","id":1360707,"title":"","content":"I don't have my PDFs handy, but I'm pretty sure 2e Crane Style was in Glories of the Most High: the Maidens.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11237-jefepato","name":"Jefepato","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11237_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"557"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-13T11:06:33-08:00","id":1360715,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jefepato</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1360478-martial-arts-with-perfect-defenses-in-exalted-2nd-edition?p=1360707#post1360707\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't have my PDFs handy, but I'm pretty sure 2e Crane Style was in Glories of the Most High: the Maidens.</div> </div> </div> </div>God bless you.<br /> <br /> I have wasted hours today, looking through my books for it. For some reason I thought it was in one of the earlier 2nd Edition books or one of the Scroll of the Monk books.<br /> <br /> CROSSED WINGS DENIAL [<u>Crane Style</u>, Glories of the Most High: The Maidens of Destiny- Page 28]<br /> &quot;This Charm may be activated in response to any physical attack of which the martial artist is aware, allowing her to make a perfect unarmed parry even against unblockable attacks.&quot;<br /> &quot;Use of this Charm prevents the martial artist from making any physical attacks on her next action as a special flaw of invulnerability.&quot;<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4428-daredevil","name":"Daredevil","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4428_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"404"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-13T11:28:20-08:00","id":1360718,"title":"","content":"Yeah, considering that you've still got access to pretty much unlimited counterattacks via Crane Charms it's not much of a flaw.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-13T19:31:47-08:00","id":1360802,"title":"","content":"2e Crane Style seems to be designed to give the user all the basic tools they need for Exalted combat (perfect defense, surprise breaker, counterattacks), in exchange for locking them into a fairly specific combat strategy. It's an interesting theme.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1360478-martial-arts-with-perfect-defenses-in-exalted-2nd-edition?p=1360718#post1360718\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, considering that you've still got access to pretty much unlimited counterattacks via Crane Charms it's not much of a flaw.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, your opponents could always ignore you, attack someone else (assuming you're not alone), and leave you standing there not doing much.<br /> <br /> ...I had to double-check, but unlike the 3e version (Mastery effect of Fluttering Cry of Warning), 2e Crane Style doesn't give any special ability to Defend Other your friends (which of course helps a lot when you're all-in on a counterattack strategy). I keep expecting to see it in one of the Charms. &gt;_&gt;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11237-jefepato","name":"Jefepato","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11237_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"557"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-13T20:59:37-08:00","id":1360809,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jefepato</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1360478-martial-arts-with-perfect-defenses-in-exalted-2nd-edition?p=1360802#post1360802\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean, your opponents could always ignore you, attack someone else (assuming you're not alone), and leave you standing there not doing much.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, you could use a Defend Other on your action. Or any number of miscellaneous actions (or Miscellaneous Actions).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jefepato</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1360478-martial-arts-with-perfect-defenses-in-exalted-2nd-edition?p=1360802#post1360802\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...I had to double-check, but unlike the 3e version (Mastery effect of Fluttering Cry of Warning), 2e Crane Style doesn't give any special ability to Defend Other your friends (which of course helps a lot when you're all-in on a counterattack strategy).</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure, but you could just Defend Other them normally..<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}